      "ticket": {
        "key": "AUT-8343",
        "summary": "Autofill 3.1(d) from GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco to fix missing RCM liability",
        "description": "## Description\n\nRight now, when a user reconciles their GSTR-2B with the Purchase Register and accepts invoices that are \"Not in Purchase Register\", those invoices automatically get added to ITC (table 4). That part works fine.\n\nBut here's the issue — those same invoices are RCM invoices, which means the user is also supposed to declare them as a liability in table 3.1(d). That never happens automatically. The user has to manually figure out and fill 3.1(d) themselves.\n\nSo the return ends up in a broken state:\n\nITC is claimed in table 4 ✓ RCM liability in 3.1(d) is missing ✗\n\nThis is a compliance risk. The GST return is incomplete and incorrect.\n\n## User Story\n\nWe will add an inline autofill control directly inside the 3.1(d) row — so the user can choose their source and fill just that row without affecting anything else in table 3.1.\n\nThe control will have a small dropdown with two options:\n\n- Purchase register — pulls RCM invoices from the purchase register (existing behaviour, just now available at row level)\n\n- GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco — pulls invoices that the user has already accepted as \"Not in Purchase Register\" in the reco, filters only RCM-applicable ones, and fills 3.1(d) with the aggregated taxable value and tax amounts\n\n\nOnce the user selects a source and clicks Apply:\n\n- The values populate in 3.1(d)\n\n- A small label chip appears in the row showing which source was used (e.g. \"2B vs PR reco\") so the user has a clear audit trail\n\n- The dropdown and Apply button collapse — a \"Clear\" option appears if they want to reset\n\n\n[Attachment: 99e5473c-7da6-40e9-b965-540b403bb5e8]\n## Edge Cases to Handle:\n\n- **No RCM invoices found **— if the user selects \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\" but there are no accepted RCM invoices for that GSTIN and period, show a clear message like \"No accepted RCM invoices found in 2B vs PR reco for this period\". Do not silently fill zeros.\n\n- **Values already exist in 3.1(d) **— if the user has already filled 3.1(d) manually or via another autofill, show a confirmation before overwriting: \"3.1(d) already has values. Do you want to replace them?\"\n\n- **Mixed invoices in reco** — not all accepted invoices in reco are RCM. Regular invoices must be excluded. Only invoices where the supplier has marked the supply as RCM in their GSTR-1 should be picked up.\n\n\n## Acceptance Criteria:\n\n-  3.1(d) row shows an inline dropdown with exactly two options: \"Purchase register\" and \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\"\n\n-  When \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\" is selected and applied, 3.1(d) is filled with aggregated values from accepted RCM invoices in the reco for that GSTIN and period\n\n-  Non-RCM accepted invoices are excluded from the autofill\n\n-  A source chip appears in the 3.1(d) row label after autofill, showing where the data came from\n\n-  If no qualifying invoices exist, an appropriate empty state message is shown — no silent zero fill\n\n-  If 3.1(d) already has values, the user is asked to confirm before overwriting\n\n-  Clicking Clear resets 3.1(d) and restores the dropdown to its default state\n\n-  ITC in Table 4 is unaffected\n\n-  No change to rows 3.1(a), (b), (c), (e) or the global Sales register autofill button\n\n\n",
        "ac": "## Description\n\nRight now, when a user reconciles their GSTR-2B with the Purchase Register and accepts invoices that are \"Not in Purchase Register\", those invoices automatically get added to ITC (table 4). That part works fine.\n\nBut here's the issue — those same invoices are RCM invoices, which means the user is also supposed to declare them as a liability in table 3.1(d). That never happens automatically. The user has to manually figure out and fill 3.1(d) themselves.\n\nSo the return ends up in a broken state:\n\nITC is claimed in table 4 ✓ RCM liability in 3.1(d) is missing ✗\n\nThis is a compliance risk. The GST return is incomplete and incorrect.\n\n## User Story\n\nWe will add an inline autofill control directly inside the 3.1(d) row — so the user can choose their source and fill just that row without affecting anything else in table 3.1.\n\nThe control will have a small dropdown with two options:\n\n- Purchase register — pulls RCM invoices from the purchase register (existing behaviour, just now available at row level)\n\n- GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco — pulls invoices that the user has already accepted as \"Not in Purchase Register\" in the reco, filters only RCM-applicable ones, and fills 3.1(d) with the aggregated taxable value and tax amounts\n\n\nOnce the user selects a source and clicks Apply:\n\n- The values populate in 3.1(d)\n\n- A small label chip appears in the row showing which source was used (e.g. \"2B vs PR reco\") so the user has a clear audit trail\n\n- The dropdown and Apply button collapse — a \"Clear\" option appears if they want to reset\n\n\n[Attachment: 99e5473c-7da6-40e9-b965-540b403bb5e8]\n## Edge Cases to Handle:\n\n- **No RCM invoices found **— if the user selects \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\" but there are no accepted RCM invoices for that GSTIN and period, show a clear message like \"No accepted RCM invoices found in 2B vs PR reco for this period\". Do not silently fill zeros.\n\n- **Values already exist in 3.1(d) **— if the user has already filled 3.1(d) manually or via another autofill, show a confirmation before overwriting: \"3.1(d) already has values. Do you want to replace them?\"\n\n- **Mixed invoices in reco** — not all accepted invoices in reco are RCM. Regular invoices must be excluded. Only invoices where the supplier has marked the supply as RCM in their GSTR-1 should be picked up.\n\n\n## Acceptance Criteria:\n\n-  3.1(d) row shows an inline dropdown with exactly two options: \"Purchase register\" and \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\"\n\n-  When \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\" is selected and applied, 3.1(d) is filled with aggregated values from accepted RCM invoices in the reco for that GSTIN and period\n\n-  Non-RCM accepted invoices are excluded from the autofill\n\n-  A source chip appears in the 3.1(d) row label after autofill, showing where the data came from\n\n-  If no qualifying invoices exist, an appropriate empty state message is shown — no silent zero fill\n\n-  If 3.1(d) already has values, the user is asked to confirm before overwriting\n\n-  Clicking Clear resets 3.1(d) and restores the dropdown to its default state\n\n-  ITC in Table 4 is unaffected\n\n-  No change to rows 3.1(a), (b), (c), (e) or the global Sales register autofill button\n\n\n",
