      "_agent_explorer": "Now I have a comprehensive picture. Let me compile the final analysis.\n\n---\n\n## Reusable Code Analysis for AUT-8343\n\n### 1. Primary Component to Modify\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx`** (lines 1-127)\n- **What**: The component that renders Table 3.1 (including 3.1(d))\n- **Reuse**: This is the main file to modify. The 3.1(d) row (\"Inward supplies liable to Reverse Charge\") is one of the rows in the `sup_details` array rendered by this component. The inline autofill dropdown + Apply/Clear controls need to be added here, specifically for the 3.1(d) row.\n- **Key pattern**: It uses `TableWrapper` for section chrome, `getDataApi`/`postDataApi` for API calls, `useInfoViewActionsContext` for toast notifications, and renders an `AppTable` with `getColumns()`.\n\n### 2. Column Definition to Modify\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/OutwardInwardSupplies/TableColumns.tsx`** (lines 1-191)\n- **What**: Column definitions for Table 3.1\n- **Reuse**: The \"Nature of Supplies\" column's `render` function needs to be enhanced to show the inline dropdown + source chip for the 3.1(d) row specifically. Copy the conditional render pattern used in `EligibleITC/TableColumns.tsx:17-29` where `record.isHeader` and `record.isClickable` conditions differentiate rendering.\n\n### 3. **Key Reference Pattern: EligibleITC Autofill (Table 4)**\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/EligibleITC/index.tsx`** (lines 1-869)\n- **What**: The most important reference — Table 4 already has exactly the autofill dropdown pattern needed (Purchase Register / GSTR-2B / GSTR-2B vs Purchase Register)\n- **Reuse patterns**:\n  - **Autofill dropdown**: Lines 604-621 — `AppSelect` with `Select.Option` for source selection (`purchase`, `gstr-2b`, `purchase_register`)\n  - **`autoFillData` function**: Lines 428-444 — switches behavior based on selected source\n  - **`onFill2B` API call**: Lines 294-309 — `getDataApi('gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-data/', ...)`\n  - **`onUpdateTable` API call**: Lines 380-426 — `postDataApi('gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/', ...)` — this is the exact API that fetches 2B vs PR reconciliation data\n  - **API payload pattern**: `{ match_status, partial_purchase_ids, deleted_invoice_ids }`\n\n### 4. API Endpoints to Reuse\n\n| Endpoint | Method | Where Used | Purpose for This Ticket |\n|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| `gst-returns/3b/refresh-table-three-one/` | GET | `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:63` | Existing autofill from Sales register (keep as \"Purchase register\" option) |\n| `gst-returns/3b/edit-table-three-one/` | POST | `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:81` | Save edited 3.1 values after autofill |\n| `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` | POST | `EligibleITC/index.tsx:390` and `MainOptions.tsx:203` | **New for 3.1(d)**: Fetch accepted RCM invoices from 2B vs PR reco — needs a new variant or parameter to target 3.1(d) specifically |\n| `gst-returns/3b/display/` | GET | `Details/index.tsx:19` | Fetches all 3B data including `sup_details` |\n\n### 5. Existing Components to Reuse\n\n**`AppSelect`** — `@mi/components/AppSelect`\n- Used at: `EligibleITC/index.tsx:606-621`, `CommonModules/Prepare/SummaryView/Autofill.tsx:101-114`\n- For the inline autofill dropdown\n\n**`AppPopConfirm`** — `@mi/components/AppPopConfirm`\n- Used at: `EligibleITC/index.tsx:719-751`, `MainOptions.tsx:403-429`\n- For the \"3.1(d) already has values, do you want to replace?\" confirmation\n\n**`ActionsPopover`** — `@mi/entp/reco/DocumentView/Buckets/BucketTable/ActionsPopover`\n- File: `libs/entp/src/lib/reconcile/DocumentView/Buckets/BucketTable/ActionsPopover/index.tsx`\n- A `Popconfirm` wrapper with radio group selection and confirm/cancel. Could be used as-is for the two-option source selector.\n\n**`AppStatusBadge`** — `@mi/components/AppStatusBadge`\n- File: `libs/components/src/lib/AppStatusBadge/index.tsx`\n- For the source chip label (e.g., \"2B vs PR reco\" / \"Purchase register\")\n\n**`AppTable`** — `@mi/shared/AppTable`\n- Already used in `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:115`\n\n**`TableWrapper`** — `../TableWrapper`\n- File: `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/TableWrapper.tsx`\n- Already wraps table 3.1. Supports `actions` prop (line 13) for custom controls — but the autofill needs to be inline in the row, not in the header.\n\n### 6. Types to Reuse\n\n**`libs/constants/src/models/GstReturns/3B/index.ts`**\n- `ThreeBItemProps` (line 33-47): Row data type with `nature_of_supplies`, `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess`. The 3.1(d) row is identified by its `nature_of_supplies` value.\n- `ThreeBDetailsProps` (line 66-84): API response wrapper — `sup_details` is the array containing 3.1 rows\n- `ThreeBCommonProps` (line 93-98): Common params (gstin, ret_period, upload_status, return_status)\n- `ThreeBFillFromProps` (line 1-5): Response from `fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` — contains `table_data`, `table_4_mapping`, `invoices_data`\n\n**`libs/constants/src/models/Reconcile/Buckets.ts`** (line 228)\n- `reverse_charge?: string` — field on bucket/invoice records indicating RCM\n\n### 7. Styled Components to Reuse\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/TableWrapper.styled.tsx`**\n- `StyledInputNumber` (line 21-26): Already used in table cells\n- `StyledSelect` (line 40-47): Styled Select for table cells\n- `StyledCard`, `StyledRow`, `StyledInnerBody`: Table wrapper styles\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/index.styled.tsx`**\n- `Container`, `ThreeBActionContainer`: Layout styles for action buttons\n\n### 8. Hooks and API Utilities\n\n**`@mi/hooks/APIHooks`** — `getDataApi`, `postDataApi`, `useGetDataApi`\n- Used throughout: `EligibleITC/index.tsx:13`, `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:12`, `MainOptions.tsx:23`\n\n**`@mi/context/AppInfoViewContextProvider`** — `useInfoViewActionsContext`\n- For `infoViewContext.showMessage()` and `infoViewContext.fetchError()` — the standard toast notification pattern\n\n**`@mi/hooks/AuthHooks`** — `useCurrentBusiness`\n- Used at: `MainOptions.tsx:63`, `EligibleITC/index.tsx:140`\n\n### 9. Permissions\n\n**`libs/constants/src/permissions/app/returns/GSTR3B.tsx`**\n- `GSTR3BAccess.AutofillSalesPurchaseRegister` — permission for autofill actions (used in `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:101` and `MainOptions.tsx:334`)\n- `GSTR3BAccess.EditGSTR3B` — permission for editing (used in `TableWrapper.tsx:36`)\n\n### 10. Mixpanel Events\n\n**`libs/services/mixpanel/src/SMB/GSTModule/GSTR.ts`**\n- `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofil31` (line 271): Existing event for Table 3.1 autofill\n- `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofilfrmSales` (line 225): Autofill from sales\n- `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofilfrm2BVsPurchase` (line 236): 2B vs Purchase reco event — **reuse this for the new source option**\n- A new event should be added: e.g., `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofil31d2BReco` following the same pattern\n\n### 11. Key Data Identification — The 3.1(d) Row\n\nThe 3.1(d) row is identified by its `nature_of_supplies` value: **\"Inward supplies liable to reverse charge\"** (seen in comparison reports at `libs/entp/src/lib/reports/ComparisonReports/data.tsx:12` and `libs/entp/src/lib/reports/TaxLiabilityComparisonReports/data.tsx:12`).\n\nIn the `sup_details` array from the API, this is typically the 4th item (index 3), identifiable by matching the `nature_of_supplies` string containing \"reverse charge\" or \"3.1(d)\".\n\n### 12. Parent Orchestrator\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/index.tsx`** (lines 1-117)\n- This is the parent that passes `sup_details` data and `updateData` callback to `OutwardInwardSupplies`\n- Also passes `getCommonData()` for API params (gstin, ret_period, etc.)\n- The `setData` function at line 49 shows how to update `sup_details` in the parent state\n\n### Summary of Changes Needed\n\n1. **Modify** `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx` — Add autofill state, source selection dropdown, Apply/Clear logic, confirmation modal, and API call for 3.1(d) specifically\n2. **Modify** `OutwardInwardSupplies/TableColumns.tsx` — Enhance \"Nature of Supplies\" column render for 3.1(d) row to show inline dropdown + source chip\n3. **Add** new styled components in `TableWrapper.styled.tsx` for source chip\n4. **Add** a new mixpanel event in `libs/services/mixpanel/src/SMB/GSTModule/GSTR.ts`\n5. **Possibly** add a new API endpoint parameter or a new endpoint for fetching 3.1(d)-specific RCM data from 2B vs PR reco (backend work — frontend would call similar to `fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` with a parameter like `target_table: '3.1d'`)",
      "_agent_requirements": "---\n\n## Requirements — AUT-8343: Autofill 3.1(d) from GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\n\n### Functional Requirements & User Flows\n\n**Inline Autofill Control on Row 3.1(d):**\n- Add an inline dropdown control rendered **only** inside the 3.1(d) row (\"Inward Supplies Liable to RCM\") of table 3.1 in `OutwardInwardSupplies`\n- Dropdown must have exactly **two options**:\n  1. **\"Purchase register\"** — pulls RCM invoices from the purchase register (mirrors existing global refresh behaviour, scoped to this row)\n  2. **\"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\"** — pulls invoices the user accepted as \"Not in Purchase Register\" in the reconciliation, filters only RCM-applicable ones, aggregates taxable value + tax amounts into 3.1(d)\n- An **\"Apply\" button** sits next to the dropdown; clicking it triggers the autofill for the selected source\n- After Apply succeeds:\n  - `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` in the 3.1(d) row are populated with the aggregated values\n  - A **source chip/label** appears in the row (e.g. \"2B vs PR reco\" or \"Purchase register\") as an audit trail\n  - The dropdown + Apply collapse; a **\"Clear\" button** appears instead\n- Clicking **Clear** resets 3.1(d) values to zero/empty, removes the source chip, and restores the dropdown to its default unselected state\n\n**Source: \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\" flow:**\n- Call a backend endpoint (new or existing `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` scoped to table 3.1(d)) with `match_status` including `accepted` and `notprsentinpurchase`\n- Backend must filter to **only RCM invoices** — where the supplier marked the supply as RCM in their GSTR-1\n- Non-RCM accepted invoices must be excluded\n- Aggregate `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` from qualifying invoices for the current GSTIN and return period\n- Populate the 3.1(d) row with the aggregated amounts\n\n**Source: \"Purchase register\" flow:**\n- Call the existing refresh/autofill mechanism scoped to 3.1(d) only (e.g. reuse or adapt `gst-returns/3b/refresh-table-three-one/` logic but only for the RCM row)\n- Pull RCM invoices from the purchase register and aggregate into 3.1(d)\n\n---\n\n### Business Rules & Validation Logic\n\n- **RCM-only filtering**: Only invoices where the supplier has marked the supply as Reverse Charge Mechanism (RCM) in their GSTR-1 filing are eligible. Regular B2B invoices that were accepted in reco must be excluded\n- **GSTIN + Period scoping**: All queries must be scoped to the active GSTIN (`currentBusiness`) and the selected `ret_period`\n- **Overwrite confirmation**: If 3.1(d) already has non-zero values (manually entered or from a previous autofill), show a confirmation modal: _\"3.1(d) already has values. Do you want to replace them?\"_ — user must confirm before overwrite\n- **Empty result handling**: If no qualifying RCM invoices are found, display a clear message: _\"No accepted RCM invoices found in 2B vs PR reco for this period\"_. Do **not** silently fill zeros\n- **Table 4 isolation**: ITC in Table 4 must remain completely unaffected by this autofill action\n- **Table 3.1 isolation**: Rows 3.1(a), 3.1(b), 3.1(c), 3.1(e) must not be modified. The global \"Autofill using Sales register\" button in `TableWrapper` must continue to work as-is and must not be affected\n- **Enterprise-only**: Gate behind `VITE_PRODUCT_ID` for the enterprise product. No changes to SME/GST/TaxPro flows\n\n---\n\n### UI Changes\n\n| Area | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| **3.1(d) row — \"Nature of Supplies\" column** | Add an inline autofill control (dropdown + Apply button) next to the row label text. After autofill, show a source chip (e.g. `Tag` or `Badge` from Ant Design) and a Clear button |\n| **Dropdown** | Ant Design `Select` (or `AppSelect`) with two options. Placeholder: \"Select source\" |\n| **Apply button** | Ant Design `Button` (primary, small), disabled until a source is selected |\n| **Source chip** | Small `Tag` component (e.g. `<Tag color=\"blue\">2B vs PR reco</Tag>`) rendered inline in the row label after autofill |\n| **Clear button** | Link-style or ghost button to reset. Replaces dropdown+Apply after autofill |\n| **Confirmation modal** | `AppPopConfirm` or `Modal.confirm` — triggered when 3.1(d) already has values |\n| **Empty state message** | `infoViewContext.fetchError()` or inline warning message when no RCM invoices found |\n| **Loading state** | Show loader/spinner on the Apply button or row while API call is in progress |\n\n**Component hierarchy** (existing pattern from `OutwardInwardSupplies`):\n```\nOutwardInwardSupplies (index.tsx)\n  └── TableWrapper\n      └── AppTable\n          └── Row 3.1(d)\n              └── [NEW] Inline autofill control (dropdown + apply + chip + clear)\n```\n\n---\n\n### API Interactions\n\n| Operation | Endpoint | Method | Payload | Notes |\n|-----------|----------|--------|---------|-------|\n| **Autofill 3.1(d) from 2B vs PR Reco** | `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` (existing) or new `gst-returns/3b/autofill-table-three-one-d/` | POST | `{ match_status: \"accepted,notprsentinpurchase\", rcm_only: true }` | Backend must filter to RCM invoices only and return aggregated `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` |\n| **Autofill 3.1(d) from Purchase Register** | `gst-returns/3b/refresh-table-three-one/` (existing, possibly with a `row_filter` param) or new scoped endpoint | GET/POST | Scope to RCM row only | Reuse existing refresh but return only 3.1(d) data |\n| **Save 3.1(d) values** | `gst-returns/3b/edit-table-three-one/` (existing) | POST | `{ ...getCommonData(), sup_details: tableData }` | Existing save mechanism — no change needed |\n\n**Expected response shape** (for new/adapted endpoint):\n```typescript\n{\n  data: {\n    txval: number;\n    igst: number;\n    cgst: number;\n    sgst: number;\n    cess: number;\n    invoice_count: number;  // For display/validation\n  }\n}\n```\n\nUse existing API patterns: `postDataApi()` / `getDataApi()` from `@mi/helpers/APIHooks`, with `infoViewContext` for error handling.\n\n---\n\n### State Management Changes\n\nAll state is local to `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx` (follows existing React hooks pattern — no Redux):\n\n| State Variable | Type | Purpose |\n|----------------|------|---------|\n| `autofillSource` | `string \\| null` | Currently selected dropdown value (`'purchase_register'` or `'2b_pr_reco'` or `null`) |\n| `autofillApplied` | `boolean` | Whether autofill has been applied (controls chip vs dropdown visibility) |\n| `appliedSource` | `string \\| null` | Which source was used for the applied autofill (for chip label) |\n| `autofillLoading` | `boolean` | Loading state during API call |\n\n**Data flow**: On Apply → call API → on success → update the 3.1(d) row in `tableData` via `updateRecord()` → set `autofillApplied=true`, `appliedSource=selectedSource`. On Clear → reset 3.1(d) fields to 0 → set `autofillApplied=false`, `appliedSource=null`.\n\n---\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n1. **No RCM invoices found** — Show message via `infoViewContext` or inline alert. Do not fill zeros silently\n2. **3.1(d) already has values** — Show `AppPopConfirm` / `Modal.confirm` before overwriting\n3. **Mixed invoices in reco** — Backend must exclude non-RCM accepted invoices. Only invoices where supplier marked RCM in GSTR-1 are eligible\n4. **User switches source after apply** — Clear should fully reset before allowing a new source selection\n5. **Edit mode interaction** — If table is in edit mode, the autofill control should still work (it populates values that the user can then further edit before saving)\n6. **Concurrent global autofill** — If the user clicks the global \"Autofill using Sales register\" button, it should overwrite all rows including 3.1(d). The source chip should be cleared since the data source changed\n7. **API failure** — Show error via `infoViewContext.fetchError()`, keep previous values intact, leave dropdown in its pre-Apply state\n8. **Permission check** — Autofill control should respect `GSTR3BAccess.AutofillSalesPurchaseRegister` permission (existing pattern in `TableWrapper`)\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Approach\n\nModify the existing `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx` and `TableColumns.tsx` to add the inline autofill control specifically for the 3.1(d) row. Create a single new component (e.g. `Table31dAutofill.tsx`) that encapsulates the dropdown, Apply button, source chip, and Clear button — following the exact same Ant Design + styled-components patterns used in `EligibleITC/index.tsx` for its autofill dropdown. The API call should reuse the existing `postDataApi` pattern with `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` (adding an RCM-only filter param), or a new purpose-built endpoint `gst-returns/3b/autofill-table-three-one-d/` if the backend team prefers isolation. The row identification for 3.1(d) should key off the `nature_of_supplies` value (`\"Inward Supplies Liable to RCM\"`) in `TableColumns.tsx` to conditionally render the inline control only on that row. State stays local to the component — no new contexts or stores needed. The confirmation dialog for existing values should use `AppPopConfirm` consistent with other confirmation patterns in the 3B module.",
      "_agent_analysis": "---\n\n## Requirements — AUT-8343: Autofill 3.1(d) from GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\n\n### Functional Requirements & User Flows\n\n**Inline Autofill Control on Row 3.1(d):**\n- Add an inline dropdown control rendered **only** inside the 3.1(d) row (\"Inward Supplies Liable to RCM\") of table 3.1 in `OutwardInwardSupplies`\n- Dropdown must have exactly **two options**:\n  1. **\"Purchase register\"** — pulls RCM invoices from the purchase register (mirrors existing global refresh behaviour, scoped to this row)\n  2. **\"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\"** — pulls invoices the user accepted as \"Not in Purchase Register\" in the reconciliation, filters only RCM-applicable ones, aggregates taxable value + tax amounts into 3.1(d)\n- An **\"Apply\" button** sits next to the dropdown; clicking it triggers the autofill for the selected source\n- After Apply succeeds:\n  - `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` in the 3.1(d) row are populated with the aggregated values\n  - A **source chip/label** appears in the row (e.g. \"2B vs PR reco\" or \"Purchase register\") as an audit trail\n  - The dropdown + Apply collapse; a **\"Clear\" button** appears instead\n- Clicking **Clear** resets 3.1(d) values to zero/empty, removes the source chip, and restores the dropdown to its default unselected state\n\n**Source: \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\" flow:**\n- Call a backend endpoint (new or existing `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` scoped to table 3.1(d)) with `match_status` including `accepted` and `notprsentinpurchase`\n- Backend must filter to **only RCM invoices** — where the supplier marked the supply as RCM in their GSTR-1\n- Non-RCM accepted invoices must be excluded\n- Aggregate `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` from qualifying invoices for the current GSTIN and return period\n- Populate the 3.1(d) row with the aggregated amounts\n\n**Source: \"Purchase register\" flow:**\n- Call the existing refresh/autofill mechanism scoped to 3.1(d) only (e.g. reuse or adapt `gst-returns/3b/refresh-table-three-one/` logic but only for the RCM row)\n- Pull RCM invoices from the purchase register and aggregate into 3.1(d)\n\n---\n\n### Business Rules & Validation Logic\n\n- **RCM-only filtering**: Only invoices where the supplier has marked the supply as Reverse Charge Mechanism (RCM) in their GSTR-1 filing are eligible. Regular B2B invoices that were accepted in reco must be excluded\n- **GSTIN + Period scoping**: All queries must be scoped to the active GSTIN (`currentBusiness`) and the selected `ret_period`\n- **Overwrite confirmation**: If 3.1(d) already has non-zero values (manually entered or from a previous autofill), show a confirmation modal: _\"3.1(d) already has values. Do you want to replace them?\"_ — user must confirm before overwrite\n- **Empty result handling**: If no qualifying RCM invoices are found, display a clear message: _\"No accepted RCM invoices found in 2B vs PR reco for this period\"_. Do **not** silently fill zeros\n- **Table 4 isolation**: ITC in Table 4 must remain completely unaffected by this autofill action\n- **Table 3.1 isolation**: Rows 3.1(a), 3.1(b), 3.1(c), 3.1(e) must not be modified. The global \"Autofill using Sales register\" button in `TableWrapper` must continue to work as-is and must not be affected\n- **Enterprise-only**: Gate behind `VITE_PRODUCT_ID` for the enterprise product. No changes to SME/GST/TaxPro flows\n\n---\n\n### UI Changes\n\n| Area | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| **3.1(d) row — \"Nature of Supplies\" column** | Add an inline autofill control (dropdown + Apply button) next to the row label text. After autofill, show a source chip (e.g. `Tag` or `Badge` from Ant Design) and a Clear button |\n| **Dropdown** | Ant Design `Select` (or `AppSelect`) with two options. Placeholder: \"Select source\" |\n| **Apply button** | Ant Design `Button` (primary, small), disabled until a source is selected |\n| **Source chip** | Small `Tag` component (e.g. `<Tag color=\"blue\">2B vs PR reco</Tag>`) rendered inline in the row label after autofill |\n| **Clear button** | Link-style or ghost button to reset. Replaces dropdown+Apply after autofill |\n| **Confirmation modal** | `AppPopConfirm` or `Modal.confirm` — triggered when 3.1(d) already has values |\n| **Empty state message** | `infoViewContext.fetchError()` or inline warning message when no RCM invoices found |\n| **Loading state** | Show loader/spinner on the Apply button or row while API call is in progress |\n\n**Component hierarchy** (existing pattern from `OutwardInwardSupplies`):\n```\nOutwardInwardSupplies (index.tsx)\n  └── TableWrapper\n      └── AppTable\n          └── Row 3.1(d)\n              └── [NEW] Inline autofill control (dropdown + apply + chip + clear)\n```\n\n---\n\n### API Interactions\n\n| Operation | Endpoint | Method | Payload | Notes |\n|-----------|----------|--------|---------|-------|\n| **Autofill 3.1(d) from 2B vs PR Reco** | `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` (existing) or new `gst-returns/3b/autofill-table-three-one-d/` | POST | `{ match_status: \"accepted,notprsentinpurchase\", rcm_only: true }` | Backend must filter to RCM invoices only and return aggregated `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` |\n| **Autofill 3.1(d) from Purchase Register** | `gst-returns/3b/refresh-table-three-one/` (existing, possibly with a `row_filter` param) or new scoped endpoint | GET/POST | Scope to RCM row only | Reuse existing refresh but return only 3.1(d) data |\n| **Save 3.1(d) values** | `gst-returns/3b/edit-table-three-one/` (existing) | POST | `{ ...getCommonData(), sup_details: tableData }` | Existing save mechanism — no change needed |\n\n**Expected response shape** (for new/adapted endpoint):\n```typescript\n{\n  data: {\n    txval: number;\n    igst: number;\n    cgst: number;\n    sgst: number;\n    cess: number;\n    invoice_count: number;  // For display/validation\n  }\n}\n```\n\nUse existing API patterns: `postDataApi()` / `getDataApi()` from `@mi/helpers/APIHooks`, with `infoViewContext` for error handling.\n\n---\n\n### State Management Changes\n\nAll state is local to `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx` (follows existing React hooks pattern — no Redux):\n\n| State Variable | Type | Purpose |\n|----------------|------|---------|\n| `autofillSource` | `string \\| null` | Currently selected dropdown value (`'purchase_register'` or `'2b_pr_reco'` or `null`) |\n| `autofillApplied` | `boolean` | Whether autofill has been applied (controls chip vs dropdown visibility) |\n| `appliedSource` | `string \\| null` | Which source was used for the applied autofill (for chip label) |\n| `autofillLoading` | `boolean` | Loading state during API call |\n\n**Data flow**: On Apply → call API → on success → update the 3.1(d) row in `tableData` via `updateRecord()` → set `autofillApplied=true`, `appliedSource=selectedSource`. On Clear → reset 3.1(d) fields to 0 → set `autofillApplied=false`, `appliedSource=null`.\n\n---\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n1. **No RCM invoices found** — Show message via `infoViewContext` or inline alert. Do not fill zeros silently\n2. **3.1(d) already has values** — Show `AppPopConfirm` / `Modal.confirm` before overwriting\n3. **Mixed invoices in reco** — Backend must exclude non-RCM accepted invoices. Only invoices where supplier marked RCM in GSTR-1 are eligible\n4. **User switches source after apply** — Clear should fully reset before allowing a new source selection\n5. **Edit mode interaction** — If table is in edit mode, the autofill control should still work (it populates values that the user can then further edit before saving)\n6. **Concurrent global autofill** — If the user clicks the global \"Autofill using Sales register\" button, it should overwrite all rows including 3.1(d). The source chip should be cleared since the data source changed\n7. **API failure** — Show error via `infoViewContext.fetchError()`, keep previous values intact, leave dropdown in its pre-Apply state\n8. **Permission check** — Autofill control should respect `GSTR3BAccess.AutofillSalesPurchaseRegister` permission (existing pattern in `TableWrapper`)\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Approach\n\nModify the existing `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx` and `TableColumns.tsx` to add the inline autofill control specifically for the 3.1(d) row. Create a single new component (e.g. `Table31dAutofill.tsx`) that encapsulates the dropdown, Apply button, source chip, and Clear button — following the exact same Ant Design + styled-components patterns used in `EligibleITC/index.tsx` for its autofill dropdown. The API call should reuse the existing `postDataApi` pattern with `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` (adding an RCM-only filter param), or a new purpose-built endpoint `gst-returns/3b/autofill-table-three-one-d/` if the backend team prefers isolation. The row identification for 3.1(d) should key off the `nature_of_supplies` value (`\"Inward Supplies Liable to RCM\"`) in `TableColumns.tsx` to conditionally render the inline control only on that row. State stays local to the component — no new contexts or stores needed. The confirmation dialog for existing values should use `AppPopConfirm` consistent with other confirmation patterns in the 3B module.\n\nNow I have a comprehensive picture. Let me compile the final analysis.\n\n---\n\n## Reusable Code Analysis for AUT-8343\n\n### 1. Primary Component to Modify\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx`** (lines 1-127)\n- **What**: The component that renders Table 3.1 (including 3.1(d))\n- **Reuse**: This is the main file to modify. The 3.1(d) row (\"Inward supplies liable to Reverse Charge\") is one of the rows in the `sup_details` array rendered by this component. The inline autofill dropdown + Apply/Clear controls need to be added here, specifically for the 3.1(d) row.\n- **Key pattern**: It uses `TableWrapper` for section chrome, `getDataApi`/`postDataApi` for API calls, `useInfoViewActionsContext` for toast notifications, and renders an `AppTable` with `getColumns()`.\n\n### 2. Column Definition to Modify\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/OutwardInwardSupplies/TableColumns.tsx`** (lines 1-191)\n- **What**: Column definitions for Table 3.1\n- **Reuse**: The \"Nature of Supplies\" column's `render` function needs to be enhanced to show the inline dropdown + source chip for the 3.1(d) row specifically. Copy the conditional render pattern used in `EligibleITC/TableColumns.tsx:17-29` where `record.isHeader` and `record.isClickable` conditions differentiate rendering.\n\n### 3. **Key Reference Pattern: EligibleITC Autofill (Table 4)**\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/EligibleITC/index.tsx`** (lines 1-869)\n- **What**: The most important reference — Table 4 already has exactly the autofill dropdown pattern needed (Purchase Register / GSTR-2B / GSTR-2B vs Purchase Register)\n- **Reuse patterns**:\n  - **Autofill dropdown**: Lines 604-621 — `AppSelect` with `Select.Option` for source selection (`purchase`, `gstr-2b`, `purchase_register`)\n  - **`autoFillData` function**: Lines 428-444 — switches behavior based on selected source\n  - **`onFill2B` API call**: Lines 294-309 — `getDataApi('gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-data/', ...)`\n  - **`onUpdateTable` API call**: Lines 380-426 — `postDataApi('gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/', ...)` — this is the exact API that fetches 2B vs PR reconciliation data\n  - **API payload pattern**: `{ match_status, partial_purchase_ids, deleted_invoice_ids }`\n\n### 4. API Endpoints to Reuse\n\n| Endpoint | Method | Where Used | Purpose for This Ticket |\n|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| `gst-returns/3b/refresh-table-three-one/` | GET | `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:63` | Existing autofill from Sales register (keep as \"Purchase register\" option) |\n| `gst-returns/3b/edit-table-three-one/` | POST | `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:81` | Save edited 3.1 values after autofill |\n| `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` | POST | `EligibleITC/index.tsx:390` and `MainOptions.tsx:203` | **New for 3.1(d)**: Fetch accepted RCM invoices from 2B vs PR reco — needs a new variant or parameter to target 3.1(d) specifically |\n| `gst-returns/3b/display/` | GET | `Details/index.tsx:19` | Fetches all 3B data including `sup_details` |\n\n### 5. Existing Components to Reuse\n\n**`AppSelect`** — `@mi/components/AppSelect`\n- Used at: `EligibleITC/index.tsx:606-621`, `CommonModules/Prepare/SummaryView/Autofill.tsx:101-114`\n- For the inline autofill dropdown\n\n**`AppPopConfirm`** — `@mi/components/AppPopConfirm`\n- Used at: `EligibleITC/index.tsx:719-751`, `MainOptions.tsx:403-429`\n- For the \"3.1(d) already has values, do you want to replace?\" confirmation\n\n**`ActionsPopover`** — `@mi/entp/reco/DocumentView/Buckets/BucketTable/ActionsPopover`\n- File: `libs/entp/src/lib/reconcile/DocumentView/Buckets/BucketTable/ActionsPopover/index.tsx`\n- A `Popconfirm` wrapper with radio group selection and confirm/cancel. Could be used as-is for the two-option source selector.\n\n**`AppStatusBadge`** — `@mi/components/AppStatusBadge`\n- File: `libs/components/src/lib/AppStatusBadge/index.tsx`\n- For the source chip label (e.g., \"2B vs PR reco\" / \"Purchase register\")\n\n**`AppTable`** — `@mi/shared/AppTable`\n- Already used in `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:115`\n\n**`TableWrapper`** — `../TableWrapper`\n- File: `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/TableWrapper.tsx`\n- Already wraps table 3.1. Supports `actions` prop (line 13) for custom controls — but the autofill needs to be inline in the row, not in the header.\n\n### 6. Types to Reuse\n\n**`libs/constants/src/models/GstReturns/3B/index.ts`**\n- `ThreeBItemProps` (line 33-47): Row data type with `nature_of_supplies`, `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess`. The 3.1(d) row is identified by its `nature_of_supplies` value.\n- `ThreeBDetailsProps` (line 66-84): API response wrapper — `sup_details` is the array containing 3.1 rows\n- `ThreeBCommonProps` (line 93-98): Common params (gstin, ret_period, upload_status, return_status)\n- `ThreeBFillFromProps` (line 1-5): Response from `fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` — contains `table_data`, `table_4_mapping`, `invoices_data`\n\n**`libs/constants/src/models/Reconcile/Buckets.ts`** (line 228)\n- `reverse_charge?: string` — field on bucket/invoice records indicating RCM\n\n### 7. Styled Components to Reuse\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/TableWrapper.styled.tsx`**\n- `StyledInputNumber` (line 21-26): Already used in table cells\n- `StyledSelect` (line 40-47): Styled Select for table cells\n- `StyledCard`, `StyledRow`, `StyledInnerBody`: Table wrapper styles\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/index.styled.tsx`**\n- `Container`, `ThreeBActionContainer`: Layout styles for action buttons\n\n### 8. Hooks and API Utilities\n\n**`@mi/hooks/APIHooks`** — `getDataApi`, `postDataApi`, `useGetDataApi`\n- Used throughout: `EligibleITC/index.tsx:13`, `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:12`, `MainOptions.tsx:23`\n\n**`@mi/context/AppInfoViewContextProvider`** — `useInfoViewActionsContext`\n- For `infoViewContext.showMessage()` and `infoViewContext.fetchError()` — the standard toast notification pattern\n\n**`@mi/hooks/AuthHooks`** — `useCurrentBusiness`\n- Used at: `MainOptions.tsx:63`, `EligibleITC/index.tsx:140`\n\n### 9. Permissions\n\n**`libs/constants/src/permissions/app/returns/GSTR3B.tsx`**\n- `GSTR3BAccess.AutofillSalesPurchaseRegister` — permission for autofill actions (used in `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:101` and `MainOptions.tsx:334`)\n- `GSTR3BAccess.EditGSTR3B` — permission for editing (used in `TableWrapper.tsx:36`)\n\n### 10. Mixpanel Events\n\n**`libs/services/mixpanel/src/SMB/GSTModule/GSTR.ts`**\n- `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofil31` (line 271): Existing event for Table 3.1 autofill\n- `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofilfrmSales` (line 225): Autofill from sales\n- `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofilfrm2BVsPurchase` (line 236): 2B vs Purchase reco event — **reuse this for the new source option**\n- A new event should be added: e.g., `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofil31d2BReco` following the same pattern\n\n### 11. Key Data Identification — The 3.1(d) Row\n\nThe 3.1(d) row is identified by its `nature_of_supplies` value: **\"Inward supplies liable to reverse charge\"** (seen in comparison reports at `libs/entp/src/lib/reports/ComparisonReports/data.tsx:12` and `libs/entp/src/lib/reports/TaxLiabilityComparisonReports/data.tsx:12`).\n\nIn the `sup_details` array from the API, this is typically the 4th item (index 3), identifiable by matching the `nature_of_supplies` string containing \"reverse charge\" or \"3.1(d)\".\n\n### 12. Parent Orchestrator\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/index.tsx`** (lines 1-117)\n- This is the parent that passes `sup_details` data and `updateData` callback to `OutwardInwardSupplies`\n- Also passes `getCommonData()` for API params (gstin, ret_period, etc.)\n- The `setData` function at line 49 shows how to update `sup_details` in the parent state\n\n### Summary of Changes Needed\n\n1. **Modify** `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx` — Add autofill state, source selection dropdown, Apply/Clear logic, confirmation modal, and API call for 3.1(d) specifically\n2. **Modify** `OutwardInwardSupplies/TableColumns.tsx` — Enhance \"Nature of Supplies\" column render for 3.1(d) row to show inline dropdown + source chip\n3. **Add** new styled components in `TableWrapper.styled.tsx` for source chip\n4. **Add** a new mixpanel event in `libs/services/mixpanel/src/SMB/GSTModule/GSTR.ts`\n5. **Possibly** add a new API endpoint parameter or a new endpoint for fetching 3.1(d)-specific RCM data from 2B vs PR reco (backend work — frontend would call similar to `fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` with a parameter like `target_table: '3.1d'`)\n\nError: Reached max turns (4)",
      "explore_plan": "The 4 OpenSpec artifacts are complete. Here's a summary of what was produced:\n\n**Proposal** — Establishes that RCM liability in 3.1(d) is never auto-filled when users accept \"Not in Purchase Register\" invoices in reconciliation, creating compliance risk. Introduces one new capability: `table-31d-inline-autofill`.\n\n**Design** — 6 key decisions: inline control in the \"Nature of Supplies\" column cell (D1), encapsulated `Table31dAutofill` component (D2), reuse `fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` endpoint with RCM-only params (D3), local state in `OutwardInwardSupplies` (D4), Ant Design `Tag` for source chip (D5), `Modal.confirm` for overwrite dialog (D6).\n\n**Specs** — 11 requirements with 19 WHEN/THEN scenarios covering: inline control rendering, dropdown options, 2B-vs-PR-reco autofill, purchase-register autofill, source chip display, Clear reset, empty result handling, overwrite confirmation, API error handling, permission gating, global refresh interaction, and Mixpanel tracking.\n\n**Tasks** — 8 task groups with 24 checkboxed tasks ordered by dependency: types/constants → mixpanel events → styled components → core `Table31dAutofill` component → `OutwardInwardSupplies` state/API logic → `TableColumns` conditional render → tests → verification.",
      "explore_openspec": null,
      "explore_agents": {
        "analysis": "---\n\n## Requirements — AUT-8343: Autofill 3.1(d) from GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\n\n### Functional Requirements & User Flows\n\n**Inline Autofill Control on Row 3.1(d):**\n- Add an inline dropdown control rendered **only** inside the 3.1(d) row (\"Inward Supplies Liable to RCM\") of table 3.1 in `OutwardInwardSupplies`\n- Dropdown must have exactly **two options**:\n  1. **\"Purchase register\"** — pulls RCM invoices from the purchase register (mirrors existing global refresh behaviour, scoped to this row)\n  2. **\"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\"** — pulls invoices the user accepted as \"Not in Purchase Register\" in the reconciliation, filters only RCM-applicable ones, aggregates taxable value + tax amounts into 3.1(d)\n- An **\"Apply\" button** sits next to the dropdown; clicking it triggers the autofill for the selected source\n- After Apply succeeds:\n  - `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` in the 3.1(d) row are populated with the aggregated values\n  - A **source chip/label** appears in the row (e.g. \"2B vs PR reco\" or \"Purchase register\") as an audit trail\n  - The dropdown + Apply collapse; a **\"Clear\" button** appears instead\n- Clicking **Clear** resets 3.1(d) values to zero/empty, removes the source chip, and restores the dropdown to its default unselected state\n\n**Source: \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\" flow:**\n- Call a backend endpoint (new or existing `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` scoped to table 3.1(d)) with `match_status` including `accepted` and `notprsentinpurchase`\n- Backend must filter to **only RCM invoices** — where the supplier marked the supply as RCM in their GSTR-1\n- Non-RCM accepted invoices must be excluded\n- Aggregate `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` from qualifying invoices for the current GSTIN and return period\n- Populate the 3.1(d) row with the aggregated amounts\n\n**Source: \"Purchase register\" flow:**\n- Call the existing refresh/autofill mechanism scoped to 3.1(d) only (e.g. reuse or adapt `gst-returns/3b/refresh-table-three-one/` logic but only for the RCM row)\n- Pull RCM invoices from the purchase register and aggregate into 3.1(d)\n\n---\n\n### Business Rules & Validation Logic\n\n- **RCM-only filtering**: Only invoices where the supplier has marked the supply as Reverse Charge Mechanism (RCM) in their GSTR-1 filing are eligible. Regular B2B invoices that were accepted in reco must be excluded\n- **GSTIN + Period scoping**: All queries must be scoped to the active GSTIN (`currentBusiness`) and the selected `ret_period`\n- **Overwrite confirmation**: If 3.1(d) already has non-zero values (manually entered or from a previous autofill), show a confirmation modal: _\"3.1(d) already has values. Do you want to replace them?\"_ — user must confirm before overwrite\n- **Empty result handling**: If no qualifying RCM invoices are found, display a clear message: _\"No accepted RCM invoices found in 2B vs PR reco for this period\"_. Do **not** silently fill zeros\n- **Table 4 isolation**: ITC in Table 4 must remain completely unaffected by this autofill action\n- **Table 3.1 isolation**: Rows 3.1(a), 3.1(b), 3.1(c), 3.1(e) must not be modified. The global \"Autofill using Sales register\" button in `TableWrapper` must continue to work as-is and must not be affected\n- **Enterprise-only**: Gate behind `VITE_PRODUCT_ID` for the enterprise product. No changes to SME/GST/TaxPro flows\n\n---\n\n### UI Changes\n\n| Area | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| **3.1(d) row — \"Nature of Supplies\" column** | Add an inline autofill control (dropdown + Apply button) next to the row label text. After autofill, show a source chip (e.g. `Tag` or `Badge` from Ant Design) and a Clear button |\n| **Dropdown** | Ant Design `Select` (or `AppSelect`) with two options. Placeholder: \"Select source\" |\n| **Apply button** | Ant Design `Button` (primary, small), disabled until a source is selected |\n| **Source chip** | Small `Tag` component (e.g. `<Tag color=\"blue\">2B vs PR reco</Tag>`) rendered inline in the row label after autofill |\n| **Clear button** | Link-style or ghost button to reset. Replaces dropdown+Apply after autofill |\n| **Confirmation modal** | `AppPopConfirm` or `Modal.confirm` — triggered when 3.1(d) already has values |\n| **Empty state message** | `infoViewContext.fetchError()` or inline warning message when no RCM invoices found |\n| **Loading state** | Show loader/spinner on the Apply button or row while API call is in progress |\n\n**Component hierarchy** (existing pattern from `OutwardInwardSupplies`):\n```\nOutwardInwardSupplies (index.tsx)\n  └── TableWrapper\n      └── AppTable\n          └── Row 3.1(d)\n              └── [NEW] Inline autofill control (dropdown + apply + chip + clear)\n```\n\n---\n\n### API Interactions\n\n| Operation | Endpoint | Method | Payload | Notes |\n|-----------|----------|--------|---------|-------|\n| **Autofill 3.1(d) from 2B vs PR Reco** | `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` (existing) or new `gst-returns/3b/autofill-table-three-one-d/` | POST | `{ match_status: \"accepted,notprsentinpurchase\", rcm_only: true }` | Backend must filter to RCM invoices only and return aggregated `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` |\n| **Autofill 3.1(d) from Purchase Register** | `gst-returns/3b/refresh-table-three-one/` (existing, possibly with a `row_filter` param) or new scoped endpoint | GET/POST | Scope to RCM row only | Reuse existing refresh but return only 3.1(d) data |\n| **Save 3.1(d) values** | `gst-returns/3b/edit-table-three-one/` (existing) | POST | `{ ...getCommonData(), sup_details: tableData }` | Existing save mechanism — no change needed |\n\n**Expected response shape** (for new/adapted endpoint):\n```typescript\n{\n  data: {\n    txval: number;\n    igst: number;\n    cgst: number;\n    sgst: number;\n    cess: number;\n    invoice_count: number;  // For display/validation\n  }\n}\n```\n\nUse existing API patterns: `postDataApi()` / `getDataApi()` from `@mi/helpers/APIHooks`, with `infoViewContext` for error handling.\n\n---\n\n### State Management Changes\n\nAll state is local to `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx` (follows existing React hooks pattern — no Redux):\n\n| State Variable | Type | Purpose |\n|----------------|------|---------|\n| `autofillSource` | `string \\| null` | Currently selected dropdown value (`'purchase_register'` or `'2b_pr_reco'` or `null`) |\n| `autofillApplied` | `boolean` | Whether autofill has been applied (controls chip vs dropdown visibility) |\n| `appliedSource` | `string \\| null` | Which source was used for the applied autofill (for chip label) |\n| `autofillLoading` | `boolean` | Loading state during API call |\n\n**Data flow**: On Apply → call API → on success → update the 3.1(d) row in `tableData` via `updateRecord()` → set `autofillApplied=true`, `appliedSource=selectedSource`. On Clear → reset 3.1(d) fields to 0 → set `autofillApplied=false`, `appliedSource=null`.\n\n---\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n1. **No RCM invoices found** — Show message via `infoViewContext` or inline alert. Do not fill zeros silently\n2. **3.1(d) already has values** — Show `AppPopConfirm` / `Modal.confirm` before overwriting\n3. **Mixed invoices in reco** — Backend must exclude non-RCM accepted invoices. Only invoices where supplier marked RCM in GSTR-1 are eligible\n4. **User switches source after apply** — Clear should fully reset before allowing a new source selection\n5. **Edit mode interaction** — If table is in edit mode, the autofill control should still work (it populates values that the user can then further edit before saving)\n6. **Concurrent global autofill** — If the user clicks the global \"Autofill using Sales register\" button, it should overwrite all rows including 3.1(d). The source chip should be cleared since the data source changed\n7. **API failure** — Show error via `infoViewContext.fetchError()`, keep previous values intact, leave dropdown in its pre-Apply state\n8. **Permission check** — Autofill control should respect `GSTR3BAccess.AutofillSalesPurchaseRegister` permission (existing pattern in `TableWrapper`)\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Approach\n\nModify the existing `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx` and `TableColumns.tsx` to add the inline autofill control specifically for the 3.1(d) row. Create a single new component (e.g. `Table31dAutofill.tsx`) that encapsulates the dropdown, Apply button, source chip, and Clear button — following the exact same Ant Design + styled-components patterns used in `EligibleITC/index.tsx` for its autofill dropdown. The API call should reuse the existing `postDataApi` pattern with `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` (adding an RCM-only filter param), or a new purpose-built endpoint `gst-returns/3b/autofill-table-three-one-d/` if the backend team prefers isolation. The row identification for 3.1(d) should key off the `nature_of_supplies` value (`\"Inward Supplies Liable to RCM\"`) in `TableColumns.tsx` to conditionally render the inline control only on that row. State stays local to the component — no new contexts or stores needed. The confirmation dialog for existing values should use `AppPopConfirm` consistent with other confirmation patterns in the 3B module.\n\nNow I have a comprehensive picture. Let me compile the final analysis.\n\n---\n\n## Reusable Code Analysis for AUT-8343\n\n### 1. Primary Component to Modify\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx`** (lines 1-127)\n- **What**: The component that renders Table 3.1 (including 3.1(d))\n- **Reuse**: This is the main file to modify. The 3.1(d) row (\"Inward supplies liable to Reverse Charge\") is one of the rows in the `sup_details` array rendered by this component. The inline autofill dropdown + Apply/Clear controls need to be added here, specifically for the 3.1(d) row.\n- **Key pattern**: It uses `TableWrapper` for section chrome, `getDataApi`/`postDataApi` for API calls, `useInfoViewActionsContext` for toast notifications, and renders an `AppTable` with `getColumns()`.\n\n### 2. Column Definition to Modify\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/OutwardInwardSupplies/TableColumns.tsx`** (lines 1-191)\n- **What**: Column definitions for Table 3.1\n- **Reuse**: The \"Nature of Supplies\" column's `render` function needs to be enhanced to show the inline dropdown + source chip for the 3.1(d) row specifically. Copy the conditional render pattern used in `EligibleITC/TableColumns.tsx:17-29` where `record.isHeader` and `record.isClickable` conditions differentiate rendering.\n\n### 3. **Key Reference Pattern: EligibleITC Autofill (Table 4)**\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/EligibleITC/index.tsx`** (lines 1-869)\n- **What**: The most important reference — Table 4 already has exactly the autofill dropdown pattern needed (Purchase Register / GSTR-2B / GSTR-2B vs Purchase Register)\n- **Reuse patterns**:\n  - **Autofill dropdown**: Lines 604-621 — `AppSelect` with `Select.Option` for source selection (`purchase`, `gstr-2b`, `purchase_register`)\n  - **`autoFillData` function**: Lines 428-444 — switches behavior based on selected source\n  - **`onFill2B` API call**: Lines 294-309 — `getDataApi('gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-data/', ...)`\n  - **`onUpdateTable` API call**: Lines 380-426 — `postDataApi('gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/', ...)` — this is the exact API that fetches 2B vs PR reconciliation data\n  - **API payload pattern**: `{ match_status, partial_purchase_ids, deleted_invoice_ids }`\n\n### 4. API Endpoints to Reuse\n\n| Endpoint | Method | Where Used | Purpose for This Ticket |\n|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| `gst-returns/3b/refresh-table-three-one/` | GET | `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:63` | Existing autofill from Sales register (keep as \"Purchase register\" option) |\n| `gst-returns/3b/edit-table-three-one/` | POST | `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:81` | Save edited 3.1 values after autofill |\n| `gst-returns/3b/fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` | POST | `EligibleITC/index.tsx:390` and `MainOptions.tsx:203` | **New for 3.1(d)**: Fetch accepted RCM invoices from 2B vs PR reco — needs a new variant or parameter to target 3.1(d) specifically |\n| `gst-returns/3b/display/` | GET | `Details/index.tsx:19` | Fetches all 3B data including `sup_details` |\n\n### 5. Existing Components to Reuse\n\n**`AppSelect`** — `@mi/components/AppSelect`\n- Used at: `EligibleITC/index.tsx:606-621`, `CommonModules/Prepare/SummaryView/Autofill.tsx:101-114`\n- For the inline autofill dropdown\n\n**`AppPopConfirm`** — `@mi/components/AppPopConfirm`\n- Used at: `EligibleITC/index.tsx:719-751`, `MainOptions.tsx:403-429`\n- For the \"3.1(d) already has values, do you want to replace?\" confirmation\n\n**`ActionsPopover`** — `@mi/entp/reco/DocumentView/Buckets/BucketTable/ActionsPopover`\n- File: `libs/entp/src/lib/reconcile/DocumentView/Buckets/BucketTable/ActionsPopover/index.tsx`\n- A `Popconfirm` wrapper with radio group selection and confirm/cancel. Could be used as-is for the two-option source selector.\n\n**`AppStatusBadge`** — `@mi/components/AppStatusBadge`\n- File: `libs/components/src/lib/AppStatusBadge/index.tsx`\n- For the source chip label (e.g., \"2B vs PR reco\" / \"Purchase register\")\n\n**`AppTable`** — `@mi/shared/AppTable`\n- Already used in `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:115`\n\n**`TableWrapper`** — `../TableWrapper`\n- File: `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/TableWrapper.tsx`\n- Already wraps table 3.1. Supports `actions` prop (line 13) for custom controls — but the autofill needs to be inline in the row, not in the header.\n\n### 6. Types to Reuse\n\n**`libs/constants/src/models/GstReturns/3B/index.ts`**\n- `ThreeBItemProps` (line 33-47): Row data type with `nature_of_supplies`, `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess`. The 3.1(d) row is identified by its `nature_of_supplies` value.\n- `ThreeBDetailsProps` (line 66-84): API response wrapper — `sup_details` is the array containing 3.1 rows\n- `ThreeBCommonProps` (line 93-98): Common params (gstin, ret_period, upload_status, return_status)\n- `ThreeBFillFromProps` (line 1-5): Response from `fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` — contains `table_data`, `table_4_mapping`, `invoices_data`\n\n**`libs/constants/src/models/Reconcile/Buckets.ts`** (line 228)\n- `reverse_charge?: string` — field on bucket/invoice records indicating RCM\n\n### 7. Styled Components to Reuse\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/TableWrapper.styled.tsx`**\n- `StyledInputNumber` (line 21-26): Already used in table cells\n- `StyledSelect` (line 40-47): Styled Select for table cells\n- `StyledCard`, `StyledRow`, `StyledInnerBody`: Table wrapper styles\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/index.styled.tsx`**\n- `Container`, `ThreeBActionContainer`: Layout styles for action buttons\n\n### 8. Hooks and API Utilities\n\n**`@mi/hooks/APIHooks`** — `getDataApi`, `postDataApi`, `useGetDataApi`\n- Used throughout: `EligibleITC/index.tsx:13`, `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:12`, `MainOptions.tsx:23`\n\n**`@mi/context/AppInfoViewContextProvider`** — `useInfoViewActionsContext`\n- For `infoViewContext.showMessage()` and `infoViewContext.fetchError()` — the standard toast notification pattern\n\n**`@mi/hooks/AuthHooks`** — `useCurrentBusiness`\n- Used at: `MainOptions.tsx:63`, `EligibleITC/index.tsx:140`\n\n### 9. Permissions\n\n**`libs/constants/src/permissions/app/returns/GSTR3B.tsx`**\n- `GSTR3BAccess.AutofillSalesPurchaseRegister` — permission for autofill actions (used in `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx:101` and `MainOptions.tsx:334`)\n- `GSTR3BAccess.EditGSTR3B` — permission for editing (used in `TableWrapper.tsx:36`)\n\n### 10. Mixpanel Events\n\n**`libs/services/mixpanel/src/SMB/GSTModule/GSTR.ts`**\n- `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofil31` (line 271): Existing event for Table 3.1 autofill\n- `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofilfrmSales` (line 225): Autofill from sales\n- `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofilfrm2BVsPurchase` (line 236): 2B vs Purchase reco event — **reuse this for the new source option**\n- A new event should be added: e.g., `onMPGSTR3bPrepareAutofil31d2BReco` following the same pattern\n\n### 11. Key Data Identification — The 3.1(d) Row\n\nThe 3.1(d) row is identified by its `nature_of_supplies` value: **\"Inward supplies liable to reverse charge\"** (seen in comparison reports at `libs/entp/src/lib/reports/ComparisonReports/data.tsx:12` and `libs/entp/src/lib/reports/TaxLiabilityComparisonReports/data.tsx:12`).\n\nIn the `sup_details` array from the API, this is typically the 4th item (index 3), identifiable by matching the `nature_of_supplies` string containing \"reverse charge\" or \"3.1(d)\".\n\n### 12. Parent Orchestrator\n\n**`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/3B/Details/index.tsx`** (lines 1-117)\n- This is the parent that passes `sup_details` data and `updateData` callback to `OutwardInwardSupplies`\n- Also passes `getCommonData()` for API params (gstin, ret_period, etc.)\n- The `setData` function at line 49 shows how to update `sup_details` in the parent state\n\n### Summary of Changes Needed\n\n1. **Modify** `OutwardInwardSupplies/index.tsx` — Add autofill state, source selection dropdown, Apply/Clear logic, confirmation modal, and API call for 3.1(d) specifically\n2. **Modify** `OutwardInwardSupplies/TableColumns.tsx` — Enhance \"Nature of Supplies\" column render for 3.1(d) row to show inline dropdown + source chip\n3. **Add** new styled components in `TableWrapper.styled.tsx` for source chip\n4. **Add** a new mixpanel event in `libs/services/mixpanel/src/SMB/GSTModule/GSTR.ts`\n5. **Possibly** add a new API endpoint parameter or a new endpoint for fetching 3.1(d)-specific RCM data from 2B vs PR reco (backend work — frontend would call similar to `fill-from-2b-pr-reco/` with a parameter like `target_table: '3.1d'`)\n\nError: Reached max turns (4)"
