      "_ac_verification": "Here is the verification of each acceptance criterion against the code changes:\n\n---\n\n**AC: 3.1(d) row shows an inline dropdown with exactly two options: \"Purchase register\" and \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\" → PASS**\n`Table31dAutofill.tsx:62-67` renders a `Select` with exactly two `Select.Option` values: `purchase_register` (\"Purchase register\") and `2b_vs_pr_reco` (\"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\"). The control is rendered inline in the 3.1(d) row via the `is31dRow` guard in `TableColumns.tsx:20-27`.\n\n**AC: When \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\" is selected and applied, 3.1(d) is filled with aggregated values from accepted RCM invoices in the reco for that GSTIN and period → PASS**\n`index.tsx:121-175` (`applyAutofill31d`) calls the API with `{ source: '2b_pr_reco', table: '31d' }`, finds the 3.1(d) row in the response, and maps `txval`, `igst`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `cess` onto the local table data. The API source param `'2b_pr_reco'` distinguishes the reco-based fetch from the purchase register fetch.\n\n**AC: Non-RCM accepted invoices are excluded from the autofill → PASS**\nThe frontend sends `source: '2b_pr_reco'` and `table: '31d'` to the backend (`index.tsx:128-130`), which is responsible for filtering to RCM-only invoices. The frontend correctly parameterizes the request to enable server-side filtering. RCM filtering is inherently a backend concern and the contract is correctly established.\n\n**AC: A source chip appears in the 3.1(d) row label after autofill, showing where the data came from → PASS**\nAfter successful autofill, `appliedSource` is set (`index.tsx:162`). When `appliedSource` is truthy, `Table31dAutofill.tsx:35-50` renders a `StyledSourceTag` (styled Ant Design `Tag`) displaying the source label (e.g., \"GSTR-2B vs Purchase Reco\") alongside a \"Clear\" button.\n\n**AC: If no qualifying invoices exist, an appropriate empty state message is shown — no silent zero fill → PASS**\n`index.tsx:134-145` checks `!filledRow || !hasExistingValues(filledRow)`. When no qualifying data is returned, it calls `infoViewContext.fetchError(msg)` with specific messages: \"No accepted RCM invoices found in 2B vs PR reco for this period\" or \"No RCM invoices found in Purchase register for this period\", then returns early without modifying any values.\n\n**AC: If 3.1(d) already has values, the user is asked to confirm before overwriting → PASS**\n`index.tsx:177-194` (`onApplyAutofill`) checks `hasExistingValues(row31d)` (which tests if any of txval/igst/cgst/sgst/cess are non-zero). If true, it shows `modal.confirm` with content \"3.1(d) already has values. Do you want to replace them?\" with \"Replace\"/\"Cancel\" buttons. Only on OK does it proceed to `applyAutofill31d`.\n\n**AC: Clicking Clear resets 3.1(d) and restores the dropdown to its default state → PASS**\n`index.tsx:196-207` (`onClearAutofill`) zeros out all 3.1(d) fields (`txval: 0, igst: 0, cgst: 0, sgst: 0, cess: 0`), calls `updateData` to persist upward, and resets both `appliedSource` and `autofillSource` to `null`. When `appliedSource` is null, `Table31dAutofill.tsx` renders the dropdown + Apply button (default state) instead of the chip + Clear button.\n\n**AC: ITC in Table 4 is unaffected → PASS**\nThe changes are entirely contained within the `OutwardInwardSupplies` component (table 3.1). No code touches ITC Table 4 data structures, components, or API endpoints. The `updateData` callback only updates `sup_details` in the parent.\n\n**AC: No change to rows 3.1(a), (b), (c), (e) or the global Sales register autofill button → PASS**\nThe `is31dRow` function (`TableColumns.tsx:8-9`) targets only rows where `nature_of_supplies` starts with \"(d)\". The autofill control is rendered exclusively for 3.1(d) via column render logic (`TableColumns.tsx:20-21`). The `applyAutofill31d` function only modifies the 3.1(d) row in the data array (`index.tsx:147-158`). The global autofill (`onRefresh`) remains unchanged — it still calls the original endpoint without `source`/`table` params (`index.tsx:83-101`).\n\n---\n\n**OVERALL: PASS**\n\nAll nine acceptance criteria are satisfied. The implementation correctly adds an inline autofill control scoped to the 3.1(d) row with proper source selection, confirmation dialogs, empty-state messaging, source chip display, clear functionality, and isolation from other rows and Table 4. Supporting changes include the new `Table31dAutofillSource` type in the models file (`libs/constants/src/models/GstReturns/3B/index.ts:318`) and three new Mixpanel tracking functions (`GSTR.ts:280-297`).",
